ID: B3-Ch02b-Scenario0
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility == 4 && v_reflexes < 4 || v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_agility < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility == 4 && v_reflexes == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)
#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_agility < 4) {
"What's the matter, hero?" Gontrok's lips pull back over his teeth as his boot crashes into Daren's ribs again, pinning him to the stone just as the knight tries to rise. "Isn't this where the legend defies all odds and turns the tide? Don't disappoint me now... I had such high hopes for the ballads!"

"If you want a proper duel, face me!" I snatch Daren's fallen blade from the dirt, shifting my grip on the leather hilt. "I'll make it worth your while."

"I don't know what you are, boy, but a dare is a dare," Gontrok says, turning away from Daren to tower over me. "Let's see if your hands match your mouth."

The giant surges forward. I leap backward, trying to put distance between us.

Gontrok is impossibly fast. He closes thirty feet in a single bound, iron fingers clamping around my skull before I can bring the steel up.

"Pathetic," he grunts, and drives my head into the cobblestones with the same bone-crushing force that felled Hadrik.

}
#if(v_agility == 4 && v_reflexes < 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
"What's the matter, hero?" Gontrok's lips pull back over his teeth as his boot crashes into Daren's ribs again, pinning him to the stone just as the knight tries to rise. "Isn't this where the legend defies all odds and turns the tide? Don't disappoint me now... I had such high hopes for the ballads!"

"If you want a proper duel, face me!" I snatch Daren's fallen blade from the dirt, shifting my grip on the leather hilt. "I'll make it worth your while."

"I don't know what you are, boy, but a dare is a dare," Gontrok says, turning away from Daren to tower over me. "Let's see if your hands match your mouth."

The giant surges forward. I leap backward, trying to put distance between us.

With enhanced agility, I cover ground fast, but Gontrok matches my pace stride for stride. Every time I skip away, he closes the distance in a blur, crowding my guard.

A single misplaced heel in the gravel is all he needs. His left hand shoots out, locking around my throat like an iron vise. Before I can slash, his right fist drives into my face, shattering my skull instantly.

}
#if(v_agility == 4 && v_reflexes == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
"What's the matter, hero?" Gontrok's lips pull back over his teeth as his boot crashes into Daren's ribs again, pinning him to the stone just as the knight tries to rise. "Isn't this where the legend defies all odds and turns the tide? Don't disappoint me now... I had such high hopes for the ballads!"

"If you want a proper duel, face me!" I snatch Daren's fallen blade from the dirt, shifting my grip on the leather hilt. "I'll make it worth your while."

"I don't know what you are, boy, but a dare is a dare," Gontrok says, turning away from Daren to tower over me. "Let's see if your hands match your mouth."

The giant surges forward. I leap backward, trying to put distance between us.

With enhanced agility, I cover ground fast, but Gontrok matches my pace stride for stride. Every time I skip away, he closes the distance in a blur, crowding my guard.

My maxed reflexes keep me a fraction of an inch ahead of his reach. I don't attempt an offensive strike—against a giant, an attack would open a fatal gap in my guard. I fight purely on evasion, weaving through his punches, giving him nothing to seize.

As I skip back another five paces to reset my stance, an invisible, crushing weight slams down from above, driving me flat against the cobblestones. I force my neck to turn: across the street, Leila lies pinned beside Kate and Flower. The captain has reestablished his suppression field over everyone.

"Just what do you think you're doing, captain?..." Gontrok asks, scowling over his shoulder as he approaches me.

}
