#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_reflexes < 4) {
"What's the matter, hero?" Gontrok's lips pull back over his teeth as his boot crashes into Daren's ribs again, pinning him to the stone just as the knight tries to rise. "Isn't this where the legend defies all odds and turns the tide? Don't disappoint me now... I had such high hopes for the ballads!"

"If you want a proper duel, face me!" I snatch Daren's fallen blade from the dirt, shifting my grip on the leather hilt. "I'll make it worth your while."

"I don't know what you are, boy, but a dare is a dare," Gontrok says, turning away from Daren to tower over me. "Let's see if your hands match your mouth."

The giant surges forward, but before his reach closes, I kick off the cobblestones and soar twenty feet into the air on Melindra's wind currents.

"Ah," Gontrok looks up, his grin returning. "You think taking the sky gives you an edge. You have no idea what you're dealing with."

Two massive, leathery wyvern wings erupt from Gontrok's shoulder blades with a wet, cracking pop of shifting bone. He beats the wings once, launching into the sky with terrifying speed.

Partial shapeshifting. Retaining the raw mass and durability of a giant while adopting a wyvern's aerial propulsion. So much for the height advantage.

In the air, his wingbeats far outstrip the gentle glide of Melindra's spell.

Without superhuman reflexes to read his approach, I can't compensate for the flight delay. He cuts across my line of ascent, rips his hand into my collar, and drives an iron fist straight through my face.

}
#if(v_reflexes == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
"What's the matter, hero?" Gontrok's lips pull back over his teeth as his boot crashes into Daren's ribs again, pinning him to the stone just as the knight tries to rise. "Isn't this where the legend defies all odds and turns the tide? Don't disappoint me now... I had such high hopes for the ballads!"

"If you want a proper duel, face me!" I snatch Daren's fallen blade from the dirt, shifting my grip on the leather hilt. "I'll make it worth your while."

"I don't know what you are, boy, but a dare is a dare," Gontrok says, turning away from Daren to tower over me. "Let's see if your hands match your mouth."

The giant surges forward, but before his reach closes, I kick off the cobblestones and soar twenty feet into the air on Melindra's wind currents.

"Ah," Gontrok looks up, his grin returning. "You think taking the sky gives you an edge. You have no idea what you're dealing with."

Two massive, leathery wyvern wings erupt from Gontrok's shoulder blades with a wet, cracking pop of shifting bone. He beats the wings once, launching into the sky with terrifying speed.

}
#if(v_reflexes == 4 && v_combat_technique < 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
Partial shapeshifting. Retaining the raw mass and durability of a giant while adopting a wyvern's aerial propulsion. So much for the height advantage.

In the air, his wingbeats far outstrip the gentle glide of Melindra's spell. My heightened reflexes let me duck his first two passes, but the delay in the air currents eventually catches up. He banks hard, catches my tunic in his left grip, and shatters my skull with a concussive right hook.

}
#if(v_combat_technique == 4 && v_reflexes == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
Partial shapeshifting. Retaining the raw mass and durability of a giant while adopting a wyvern's aerial propulsion. So much for the height advantage.

In the air, his wingbeats outpace Melindra's wind spell, but my combat training bridges the gap. I use tight corkscrews, stalling my lift to let him overshoot, baiting his dives and slipping beneath his wing-arcs. For nearly a minute, I lead him in an aerial spiral, neutralizing his raw mobility.

As I bank lower near the rooftops, an invisible hammer slams down from above. The force crushes me straight out of the sky, slamming me into the pavement.

Gontrok drops to the cobblestones beside me, folding his wings until the leathery membrane sinks back into his skin. He glares toward the alleyway.

"Just what do you think you're doing, captain?..." Gontrok asks.

I turn my head against the stone: Leila has been subdued, and the captain is holding the entire party flat against the ground under his crushing aura.

}
