ID: B3-Ch02b-Scenario2
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch2_serious,1)
achievement("Time to get serious",v_ac_b3_ch2_serious)

As Gontrok raises his boot over Daren, his eyes widen in sudden alarm. For the first time in the fight, his aura senses mortal peril.

In less than a second, maxed speed and strength propel me across the dust. I scoop Daren's blade from the ground and drive the point straight at the giant's heart. Gontrok twists violently aside, the steel grazing his blue uniform, and clamps his left hand around my right forearm in an iron crush.

"Attacking from behind isn't polite," Gontrok snarls, squeezing with enough force to splinter oak. "Let's ensure you never hold a blade again."

The agony is blinding, but my maxed toughness keeps the bone from snapping. Gritting my teeth through the pain, I pivot on my right foot, whipping my left heel around in a brutal spinning mule kick straight into his solar plexus. The kinetic impact rips his grip free and blasts him twelve feet backward into the dirt.

I surge forward, driving Daren's sword downward, but Gontrok rolls across the stones, the tip missing his neck by an inch. He springs to his feet and lunges. I spin inside his reach, lunging again, forcing him to leap backward before pressing in with relentless fury.

Realizing a static exchange favors his mass, I use my speed to circle him, feinting and cutting to keep him off balance. But Gontrok's reaction speed is astonishing; every dash is met with an instant counter. The ground fight stalemates, and I kick upward into the sky on Melindra's winds.

Gontrok sprouts his wyvern wings and shoots upward in pursuit.

Partial shapeshifting. What follows is a blistering dogfight above the rooftops. My aerial maneuvers and combat instincts keep Gontrok off balance, anticipating every dive and turn. Yet his thick hide and speed prevent a clean finishing strike.

As we descend near the square, the captain's invisible crushing force strikes like a dropped portcullis, smashing me into the cobblestones.

Gontrok touches down beside me, retracting his wings with a dark scowl at his superior.

"Just what do you think you're doing, captain?..." Gontrok asks.

I turn my head against the stone: Leila has been subdued, and the captain is holding the entire party flat against the ground under his crushing aura.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch02b-Concept, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02b-Concept)


ID: B3-Ch02b-Scenario3
TEXT:

"What's the matter, hero?" Gontrok's lips pull back over his teeth as his boot crashes into Daren's ribs again, pinning him to the stone just as the knight tries to rise. "Isn't this where the legend defies all odds and turns the tide? Don't disappoint me now... I had such high hopes for the ballads!"

"Damn it, Gontrok!" I shout, pointing across the plaza. "What are you doing?! Attack him now, while his back is turned!"

Gontrok halts his boot, turning with a baffled scowl. "What are you babbling about?..."

"The captain!" I yell. "Did you forget our agreement? You told us to keep him occupied so you could slit his throat and take the treasury! Well, his focus is split! Go finish him!"

"Do you honestly expect anyone to believe such a pathetic lie--" Gontrok scoffs, but an invisible weight slams down with the force of an avalanche, smashing both of us flat against the cobblestones.

Leila, Kate, and Flower are already pinned beside us, fighting for breath under the crushing field.

"What in the hell do you think you're doing, you old fossil?..." Gontrok strains against the downward pressure, teeth bared.

"Silence!" the captain snaps, his palms shaking with effort. "It takes all my concentration to sustain this containment without parsing your treason. Loyrang, step over here and slit these intruders' throats. If I shift my stance, the containment collapses."

"I told you before," Loyrang replies from his pillar, arms still crossed. "Unless the king commands it, my steel stays sheathed."

"You defy me as well?" the captain spits.

"We aren't defying you, you senile idiot!" Gontrok roars. "The tournament geas prevents us from harming Varathian citizens! How could we possibly assassinate you?!"

"These intruders carry the tournament mark as well," the captain retorts. "It didn't prevent them from assaulting the watch."

"You know what?" Gontrok says, his voice dropping into a dangerous rumble. "Maybe you're right. Maybe the whole geas is a myth to keep us docile. Let's test the theory."

Gontrok plants his palms against the stones. Veins bulge along his neck as his giant's strength battles the crushing field. The cobblestones crack beneath his hands as he heaves himself upright, step by agonizing step, his heavy boots sinking into the shattered stone under the immense downward pressure.

"Watch me!" Gontrok bellows, advancing on the captain. "Geas or no geas, I'm going to cave your skull in, you paranoid old dog! I'll show you what happens when you cross a-- wait. Did you hear that?"

Gontrok snaps his head to the right, throwing his massive palms up in a cross-block.

A split-second later, a brown-and-black blur tears through the air. Hadrik slams into Gontrok's palms like a siege engine. The shockwave of displaced air ripples across the plaza, and the kinetic blow blasts Gontrok straight through the stone wall of the nearest building.

Hadrik stands in the crater, shaking out his bruised fists: "You put me out for a minute there, Gontrok... Good thing your loud mouth was around to wake me up!"

choice("Continue", B3-Ch02b-Frail, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02b-Frail)


ID: B3-Ch02b-Concept
TEXT:

"What does it look like?" the captain says, sweat beading on his forehead. "I've immobilized the intruders. Hurry up and finish this one off so we can execute the rest. I'd do it myself, but moving risks breaking my focus."

"You sicken me," Gontrok sneers with open disgust. "I don't butcher defenseless opponents who can't raise a blade. That isn't how giants fight."

"Please tell me you're joking..." the captain mutters. "Never mind. Loyrang, step forward and execute these criminals. This barbarian cannot be reasoned with."

"I told you before," Loyrang replies from his pillar. "Unless the king commands it, my steel stays sheathed."

"Incompetents!" the captain shouts. "Do neither of you grasp the basic duties of a royal guard?!"

"If you want their blood that badly, crawl over here and spill it yourself," Gontrok says. "I won't lift a finger for your pitiful-- wait. Did you hear that?"

Gontrok snaps to his right, raising his palms in a cross-block.

Hadrik crashes in like a cannonball, punching Gontrok's palms with explosive force. The shockwave ripples across the square, and the blow launches Gontrok straight through the wall of the nearest building.

"Luckily, your captain's screeching was loud enough to wake the dead!" Hadrik roars, shaking out his bruised fists.

Gontrok pushes himself out of the rubble, brushing crushed mortar from his shoulders. "And here I thought you'd grown soft over the decades. Perhaps you can still give me a proper bout after all. Let's see what you've got, old friend."

Gontrok charges, and the two giants clash in thunderous unarmed combat. Meanwhile, the captain realizes he is on his own. Drawing a narrow, silver-hilted dagger from his sleeve, he begins shuffling toward us with agonizing slowness, carefully maintaining the crushing aura field.

We are completely pinned. Melindra cannot harm a local due to the tournament geas, and Daren's cracked ribs keep him from channeling white light to heal himself.

Arraka's voice shrieks from the golden amulet: "What is WRONG with you pathetic worms?! Is this what I've been coaching you for? To be butchered by a decrepit old man shuffling forward with a kitchen knife?! You were going to challenge the gods! How can you be so utterly useless?!"

"This decrepit old man is using the exact same crushing force as Eiden and the God of Time!" I shout back. "You expect us to treat him like an ordinary hedge wizard?!"

choice("Continue", B3-Ch02b-Teleported, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02b-Teleported)


