choice("Continue", B3-Ch02b-Teleported, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02b-Teleported)


ID: B3-Ch02b-Teleported
TEXT:

"He isn't using a spell, you cretin!" Arraka snarls. "It's aura manipulation! He expanded his aura across the entire street and compressed the weight down on you. Look—there's an obvious focal point hovering right in front of your noses to stabilize the field! Do I need to paint it for you?!"

A glowing crimson sphere of light ignites in mid-air six feet above our heads, pulsing at the epicenter of the downward pressure.

"There it is!" Arraka shrieks. "Sharpen your elements and shatter it! Now!"

Kate channels instantly, hurling a razor-sharp ice cone straight through the glowing crimson orb. The red sphere shatters with a glassy ring, and the downward pressure slackens.

Leila breaks free first, leaping forward with flashing daggers to drive the captain into defense.

As the rest of us try to stand, the air thickens again, pinning us down.

"Damn it!" Arraka curses. "He formed a secondary focal point and he's moving it erratically. I can't anchor a targeting light! This would be trivial if you morons could perceive auras on your own! At least the mute girl is keeping his hands busy!"

Leila presses the captain relentlessly, causing the suppression field to fluctuate erratically. Beside us, Hadrik and Gontrok exchange thunderous blows, the fight turning into a bloody, even brawl.

A sudden, deafening explosion echoes from the magical projection screen floating over the square.

"What was that?!" the king of Ollendor gasps in the projection, clutching his crown. "Where did that blast originate?!"

"It sounded like it came from inside the palace itself, your Majesty!" the high priest calls out.

"By the gods!" the king cries. "This must be the grave crisis our Creator foresaw!"

Eiden raises a hand. "Actually, this isn't--"

"Fear not, Creator!" the king cuts him off, pulling a brass cylinder from his pocket. "Ollendor shall demonstrate its might! I have the emergency recall device right here. One press, and every royal guard across the city is recalled to my side!"

Gontrok's eyes widen. "No... He wouldn't!"

"Cut the transmission!" the king shouts, slamming his thumb onto the trigger.

Bright pillars of teleportation light envelope the three royal guards.

"Damn it!" Gontrok roars as the white glare consumes him. "You idiot king! I can't believe--"

The light flashes and snaps shut. All three guards vanish into thin air.

The crushing downward pressure dissolves instantly. As we push ourselves up from the cobblestones, Hadrik limps over, bruised and bleeding, his left cheek swollen purple.

"So..." Hadrik mutters, wiping his split lip. "An explosion in the palace. Wonder what that was all about."

choice(""Maybe somebody else is also trying to assassinate the king."", B3-Ch02c-Assassinate, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02c-Assassinate)
choice(""Maybe Eiden tried to mess with the king, to see how he'd react."", B3-Ch02c-Mess, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02c-Mess)
choice(""Maybe it was just a defective device, and the king teleported the guards for nothing."", B3-Ch02c-Defective, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02c-Defective)
